MORE FEAR, NO TURNING BACK  \\nWE\\u2019LL LEAVE OUR NAMES ALONG THE TRACK  \\n\\nSING IT LOUD, LET THE SKY IGNITE  \\nWE\\u2019RE ALIVE, WE\\u2019RE ALIVE TONIGHT  \\nGIFTED OR NOT, WE STAND AS ONE  \\nOUR STORY\\u2019S JUST BEGUN\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true, \"1:keywords:forbidden_words\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1132"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ca2c6f51e339e8f4379c2f648ad3d35b8c56bfccf4df09e24af83dbe02489a34", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2853", "family": "ifeval-source-2853", "sample_id": "sha256:1b0a77233d9409458695ef273312d4c48dafacde20240a8066d08e48ece26041", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a poem about flooding in Donnell, TX. The poem should have a title in double angular brackets, i.e. <<title>>, and contains at least 3 words in all capital letters.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"<<When Donnell Rises>>\\n\\nRain drums hard on Donnell roofs,  \\nRed roads vanish under gray;  \\nThe creek climbs past the cotton fields,  \\nAnd carries fences far away.\\n\\nPorches hold their breath at dusk,  \\nWhile headlights tremble, pale and slow;  \\nThe **WATER** writes new maps through town,  \\nWhere **HOME** once stood in rows.\\n\\nYet neighbors lift their hands and hearts,  \\nBring bread, blankets, hope, and light;  \\nThrough **STORM**, the town stands shoulder-close\\u2014  \\nAnd dawn will find Donnell bright.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true, \"1:detectable_format:title\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2853"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

