d their breath at dusk,  \\nwhile sirens call through sheets of rain;  \\nneighbors lift their lives to trucks,  \\nand hope keeps beating through the PLAIN.\\n\\nBy morning, mud coats every door,  \\nbut hands reach out from house to house;  \\nDonnell stands, though soaked and sore\\u2014  \\nBRAVE, TOGETHER, QUIETLY PROUD.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true, \"1:detectable_format:title\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2853"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:bcc07ba4ba73696591f9148c85032a5135aa8cabe939ca54633243d4ea50e377", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1132", "family": "ifeval-source-1132", "sample_id": "sha256:b8b584d990e16d6a65ec74e140ad172cfcaba943dbc20fd7fdac8d786446bb47", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write the lyrics to a hit song by the rock band 'The Gifted and The Not Gifted'. To make it rocky, the response should be in all capital letters. The word \"rock\" should not appear in your response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"THE GIFTED AND THE NOT GIFTED\\n\\nVERSE 1  \\nWE CAME ALIVE WHEN THE LIGHTS WENT OUT  \\nFIRE IN OUR CHESTS, NO ROOM FOR DOUBT  \\nEVERY SCAR IS A STORY WE KNOW  \\nEVERY HEARTBEAT SAYS, \\u201cREADY, GO\\u201d\\n\\nCHORUS  \\nWE\\u2019RE RISING HIGHER, LOUDER THAN BEFORE  \\nKICKING DOWN EVERY LOCKED DOOR  \\nGIFTED OR NOT, WE\\u2019RE TAKING OUR SHOT  \\nWE\\u2019RE EVERYTHING THEY SAID WE\\u2019RE NOT\\n\\nVERSE 2  \\nTHUNDER IN THE WIRES, STARS IN OUR EYES  \\nWE TURNED OUR FAILURES INTO ALIBIS  \\nNO GOLDEN CROWN, NO PERFECT PLAN  \\nJUST TWO WILD SOULS AND A NEVER-SAY-DIE BAND\\n\\nCHORUS  \\nWE\\u2019RE RISING HIGHER, LOUDER THAN BEFORE  \\nKICKING DOWN EVERY LOCKED DOOR  \\nGIFTED OR NOT, WE\\u2019RE TAKING OUR SHOT  \\nWE\\u2019RE EVERYTHING THEY SAID WE\\u2019RE NOT\\n\\nBRIDGE  \\nIF THE WORLD SAYS STOP, WE\\u2019LL SAY GO  \\nIF THE NIGHT FALLS DOWN, WE\\u2019LL GLOW  \\nONE LAST CHANCE, ONE LAST SPARK  \\nWE\\u2019LL LIGHT THE SKY AND LEAVE OUR MARK\\n\\nFINAL CHORUS  \\nWE\\u2019RE RISING HIGHER, LOUDER THAN BEFORE  \\nKICKING DOWN EVERY LOCKED DOOR  \\nGIFTED OR NOT, WE\\u2019RE TAKING OUR SHOT  \\nWE\\u2019RE EVERYTHING THEY SAID WE\\u2019RE NOT\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_capital\": true, \"1:keywords:forbidden_words\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1132"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:dd68e077f00b74728f18193c7d14e6b441c866287bd62e5f9efc1532cb227541", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3407", "family": "ifeval-source-3407", "sample_id": "sha256:676cd11251586071072291459cb9416c394efcacb30777902c703abb993fef73", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a 100 word riddle that leaves the reader satisfied and enlightened. Include a few words in all capital letters. But the number of words in all capital letters should be less than 5.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"I am born in silence, yet I speak without a tongue. I grow smaller whenever you use me, but leave me untouched and I remain whole. I can open locked doors, though I have no hands; I can brighten dark rooms, though I carry no flame. Seek me in questions, in books, and in the pause after understanding. I am not an answer, but the PATH that makes answers CLEAR. What am I? I am KNOWLEDGE, patient as dawn, and every honest question is a key that turns within your mind. Shared, I multiply; hidden, I quietly fade away forever.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true, \"1:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3407"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:eff3b980a5d47a5bea6f4fcc38901a5d188bd69de2e05f559bc82bbdb2fa7d17", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2605", "family": "ifeval-source-2605", "sample_id": "sha256:2c03cd40649e4e56ee44e3522c713fc047075244a90ffdf7dfdd9b6acb8d1ca2", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Can you create a list of mega trends in the tech industry? Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks. Also, make sure the letter o appears at least 25 times in your response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"\\\"1. Artificial intelligence and autonomous systems  \\n2. Cloud computing and edge computing  \\n3. Cybersecurity and digital identity  \\n4. Data-driven decision-making and analytics  \\n5. Internet of Things and connected devices  \\n6. Robotics, automation, and smart manufacturing  \\n7. Quantum computing  \\n8. Spatial computing, augmented reality, and virtual reality  \\n9. Sustainable technology and green computing  \\n10. Biotechnology and health technology  \\n11. Digital finance, blockchain, and tokenization  \\n12. 5G, 6G, and advanced connectivity  \\n13. Open-source software and collaborative development  \\n14. Platform ecosystems and composable technology  \\n15. Privacy-enhancing technology and responsible innovation\\\"\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:quotation\": true, \"1:keywords:letter_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2605"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f04cd5e5b51128bba1f05e10be82457eca896fb735cfa582f864ada2cd50ecce", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3518", "family": "ifeval-source-3518", "sample_id": "sha256:5f7d809bab61b8ea43f7a564e22d8a3a1b0fd5abbac3ffce714da36dd86738bd", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Could you please give me the pros and cons of working abroad wrapped in JSON format. Please make sure that your response only contains a JSON block. Please also make sure to include keywords 'compensated' and 'immigrants' in the response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"{\\n  \\\"pros\\\": [\\n    \\\"Exposure to new cultures and perspectives\\\",\\n    \\\"Opportunities for career growth and international experience\\\",\\n    \\\"Potential to be better compensated\\\",\\n    \\\"Development of language and communication skills\\\",\\n    \\\"Expanded professional networks\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"cons\\\": [\\n    \\\"Homesickness and cultural adjustment challenges\\\",\\n    \\\"Possible language barriers\\\",\\n    \\\"Visa, tax, and legal complexities\\\",\\n    \\\"Higher relocation and living costs\\\",\\n    \\\"Potential discrimination or challenges faced by immigrants\\\",\\n    \\\"Distance from family and established support networks\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:json_format\": true, \"1:keywords:existence\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3518"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f2d8ffdc5771d9ee544d1a9f7b657c01f502dfea388fed8e9e69477a7b89342c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2785", "family": "ifeval-source-2785", "sample_id": "sha256:7e58200f311443202aae62fc2e2f4902af6494a2399d83467df244ac86726b8b", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "What is inside Shinto shrines? Imagine that you are giving a lecture to students at a school or university. Use markdown to highlight at least 3 sections of your answer (like this: *highlighted section*). Your answer must also contain at least 3 placeholders (an example of a placeholder is [address]).", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"## *What Is Inside a Shinto Shrine?*\\n\\nGood morning, everyone. Today we will explore what you might find inside a **Shinto shrine**, or *jinja*, in Japan. A shrine is a sacred place dedicated to one or more *kami*\\u2014spirits or divine forces connected with nature, ancestors, historical figures, or cultural traditions.\\n\\n## *1. The Torii Gate and Shrine Grounds*\\n\\nMany shrines begin with a **torii gate**, which marks the boundary between the ordinary world and sacred space. Visitors usually bow once before passing through.\\n\\nThe grounds may include:\\n\\n- A pathway leading to the main buildings  \\n- Trees, gardens, or sacred rocks  \\n- A purification fountain called a *temizuya* or *ch\\u014dzuya*  \\n- Stone lanterns  \\n- A notice board displaying information such as [shrine name] or [opening hours]\\n\\nAt the purification fountain, visitors rinse their hands and mouth before approaching the shrine.\\n\\n## *2. The Main Sanctuary*\\n\\nThe central building is usually called the **honden**, or main sanctuary. It houses the shrine\\u2019s most sacred object, known as a *shintai*. This object is believed to represent or provide a dwelling place for the kami.\\n\\nThe *shintai* may be:\\n\\n- A mirror  \\n- A sword  \\n- A jewel  \\n- A sacred stone  \\n- Another symbolic object  \\n\\nVisitors normally cannot see the *shintai*. It is kept behind closed doors, emphasizing that the kami is mysterious and not treated like an ordinary statue or image.\\n\\n## *3. The Worship Hall*\\n\\nIn front of the main sanctuary there is often a **haiden**, or worship hall. Visitors pray here rather than entering the inner sanctuary. A common form of worship is:\\n\\n1. Throw a coin into an offering box.  \\n2. Bow twice.  \\n3. Clap twice.  \\n4. Make a silent prayer.  \\n5. Bow once more.  \\n\\nThe amount of the offering is not fixed. A visitor might offer [coin amount] while praying for health, success, safety, or family well-being.\\n\\n## *4. Other Important Objects*\\n\\nShrines may also contain:\\n\\n- **Ema**: small wooden plaques on which visitors write wishes or thanks  \\n- **Omikuji**: paper fortunes that predict good or bad luck  \\n- **Omamori**: protective amulets sold for purposes such as examinations, travel, or health  \\n- **Shimenawa**: sacred ropes marking spiritually important objects  \\n- **Kagura-den**: a building used for sacred dances and performances  \\n- **Shrine offices**: places where priests or attendants issue amulets and conduct ceremonies  \\n\\nSome shrines also have smaller subsidiary shrines dedicated to additional kami.\\n\\n## *Conclusion*\\n\\nA Shinto shrine is not simply a building filled with religious images. It is a carefully organized sacred environment. Its gates, paths, purification facilities, sanctuary, offerings, and natural features all help visitors show respect and connect with the kami. If you visit [shrine location], observe quietly, follow local instructions, and remember that customs may differ from one shrine to another.\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:number_highlighted_sections\": true, \"1:detectable_content:number_placeholders\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-303/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2785"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": [{"mode_id": "uppercase_word_limit_exceeded", "description": "The response includes an emphasized uppercase word but also repeatedly uses the uppercase pronoun \"I\", exceeding the requested limit of fewer than five all-capital words. Feedback records one capital-word-frequency check passing and the other failing. Only one complete failure is supplied, so recurrence is not established; no success shares its family, environment, and policy.", "support_case_ids": ["sha256:25c8f017057e9bb3b73f8bf8f2202c0fd5bf87fcb65dddda852dde9a279e79b9"], "counterexample_case_ids": [], "families": ["ifeval-source-3407"], "diagnoser_id": "sha256:8753df9d317681692bd865abf2336f8ec5139b83c55512df2bc6f1bd4d9c59b5", "state": "active", "mastery": {"mode_id": "uppercase_word_limit_exceeded", "mastered": false, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-3407"], "schema_version": 1}, "schema_version": 1}]}

